  {"type": "split", "h2": "Mini split repair or replace", "image": "Close-up of a Midea wall-mounted ductless head, installed by EHI", "image_src": "/assets/img/work/midea-wall-head-closeup.webp", "image_fit": "cover", "image_credit": "EHI install", "image_pos": "50% 50%", "html": "<p>Repair it when the unit is under 10 years old and the fault is a drain, sensor, capacitor, fan motor, board or a leaking flare joint. Those are routine, and a cleaned, recharged mini-split runs like new.</p><p>Consider replacing when the compressor has failed on an older unit, when the outdoor unit is an early non-inverter model that struggles below freezing, or when a bargain-brand system has had a parts problem every summer. A new <a href=\"/ac/ductless-mini-split/\">Midea Hyper Heat ductless heat pump</a> starts at $5,500 installed, heats to -30°C, and cold-climate models can qualify for a rebate.</p><p>We quote both. You decide.</p>"},
